; Benchmarks live in their own stanza and do NOT ship in the main binary.
;
; That separation is load-bearing rather than tidy. bench_graph.ml contains a
; second implementation of the book's arithmetic -- a deliberate
; poll-and-recompute baseline, written so the incremental-versus-polling
; contrast can be measured instead of asserted -- and a second implementation of
; exposure and limit logic is precisely what stress.ml goes to some length to
; avoid having. Keeping it here means nothing in lib/ or bin/ can reach it.
;
; Not run by `make test` either: benchmarks take minutes and answer a different
; question from correctness.

(executable
 (name bench_graph)
 (libraries ohcamel core core_bench core_unix.command_unix)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane)))
